Root cause: merging the Dashboard/Insights branch back onto an earlier
snapshot silently reverted three files that a later branch (081c9d7,
already verified working) had built on top of. Zero frontend changes —
every fix here is backend-only, restoring exactly what routers/ai_manager.py
and main.py already expect, so the frontend's existing contract never moved.

1. app/services/auto_client.py — the merge overwrote this file with an
   OLDER version missing trigger_orchestrator_run()/AutoOperatorError/
   _get_orchestrator_config()/_format_run_result(), the exact functions
   routers/ai_manager.py imports. This alone took down the ENTIRE app —
   ai_manager.py loads at startup, so the ImportError crashed every
   route, not just AI Manager. Restored verbatim from commit 081c9d7,
   where this exact code was already live-verified (confirmed a clean
   503, not a crash, when Auto env vars are unset).

   Traced every consumer of auto_client.py first, via grep across the
   whole app/ directory — there is exactly one (routers/ai_manager.py).
   routers/disruptions.py (which would have needed a different contract,
   per earlier session notes) was never actually merged into this repo,
   so restoring the ai_manager.py-shaped version is unambiguously
   correct, not a guess between two competing needs.

2. app/main.py — ai_manager_router and insights_router were never added
   to the import list or include_router() calls, even though both
   router files exist and routers/__init__.py already exports them
   correctly. This meant /api/ai-manager/messages and /api/ai/insights
   404'd even once the ImportError above was fixed. Added both, in the
   same style/position as the existing dashboard_router registration.

3. alembic/versions/g7h8i9j0k1l2_add_last_polled_at_to_data_sources.py —
   deleted. Genuine duplicate of a2b3c4d5e6f7 (same column, same parent
   revision f6g7h8i9j0k1, different session, ten days apart) — this was
   producing 'Multiple head revisions' and crash-looping the backend
   before it could even get to the ImportError above. Confirmed via grep
   that nothing else references either file as a down_revision parent,
   so deleting one is fully safe.

VERIFIED (not just written) against a fresh checkout of this exact
commit:
- Static AST scan of every relative import in app/: 0 real breaks (2
  pre-existing deferred keycloak_admin references, unrelated, don't
  block startup).
- alembic heads: exactly one (a2b3c4d5e6f7).
- App imports and starts cleanly.
- Full pipeline re-verified end to end: create policy -> POST
  /api/orchestrator/events -> matched, routed to Workbench -> GET
  /api/workbench shows it -> POST /resolve succeeds.
- POST /api/ai-manager/messages with no Auto credentials set returns a
  clean 503 with a real error message (not 404, not 500, not a crash).
- GET /api/ai/insights -> 200. GET /api/dashboard/summary -> 200.
- git diff confirms zero files under frontend/ touched.
